dockerd must not switch containerds across restarts.

If dockerd starts while /run/containerd/containerd.sock is absent, it
supervises its own containerd and records containers in
<data-root>/containerd/daemon. Starting containerd.service afterwards
creates that socket. The next dockerd start used to treat the socket as
authoritative and attach to the system daemon, whose database is
/var/lib/containerd. Containers from the private database then disappear.

Keep supervising the private containerd when its metadata database is
already present. A fresh install still attaches to an already-running
system containerd. --containerd, or "containerd" in daemon.json, still
selects a socket explicitly.

